"1"
"Forty years I kept this"
"manor. Polished every rail."
"Now I sweep ash off marble"
"and call it dusting. The"
"family stays, so I stay."
"You're loyal.",2
"Rebuild it, then.",3
"",0
"2"
"Loyal? It's all I know. A"
"house is just walls without"
"folk who love it. I loved"
"this one. I'll love it back,"
"one swept stair at a time."
"Beautiful. Farewell.",0
"",0
"",0
"3"
"Rebuild? Oh, we shall. Stone"
"by stone, the Merrows will"
"rise again. Might take longer"
"than I have left. But my son"
"sweeps beside me now."
"Good man. Take care.",0
